{"name":"Blood Omen","hex":"#8a0303","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blood","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vital liquid flowing in the bodies of many types of animals that usually conveys nutrients and oxygen. In vertebrates, it is colored red by hemoglobin, is conveyed by arteries and veins, is pumped by the heart and is usually generated in bone marrow.","A family relationship due to birth, such as that between siblings; contrasted with relationships due to marriage or adoption. See blood relative, blood relation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause something to be covered with blood; to bloody.","To let blood (from); to bleed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blood"},{"term":"omen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something which portends or is perceived to portend either a good or evil event or circumstance in the future, or which causes a foreboding; a portent or augury.","A thing of prophetic significance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be an omen of.","To divine or predict from omens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/omen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain","blocks":[{"text":"Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain is a 1996 action-adventure video game developed by Silicon Knights and published by Crystal Dynamics for the PlayStation. A Windows port developed by Semi Logic Entertainments was released by Activision under license from Crystal Dynamics in 1997. It is the first title in the Legacy of Kain series. The game was re-released digitally via GOG.com in 2021."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7b/Blood_Omen_-_Legacy_of_Kain_Coverart.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_Omen%3A_Legacy_of_Kain","wikidata":"Q2294466"},{"title":"Blood","blocks":[{"text":"Blood is a specialized form of connective tissue and body fluid in the circulatory system of humans and other vertebrates that delivers necessary substances such as nutrients and oxygen to the cells of the body, and transports metabolic waste products away from those same cells."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Venous_and_arterial_blood.jpg/330px-Venous_and_arterial_blood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood","wikidata":"Q7873"},{"title":"Omen","blocks":[{"text":"An omen is a phenomenon that is believed to foretell the future, often signifying the advent of change. It was commonly believed in ancient history, and still believed by some today, that omens bring divine messages from the gods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Omens_%28CLIr%29.jpg/330px-Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Omens_%28CLIr%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omen","wikidata":"Q1120735"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ad/BO1-Gameplay.jpg/250px-BO1-Gameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ad/BO1-Gameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ad/BO1-Gameplay.jpg/250px-BO1-Gameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Screenshot of combat in the Battle of the Last Stand sequence. The heads-up display on the right indicates Kain's current equipment, health, and magic energy.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABO1-Gameplay.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6e/SimonTempleman.jpg/500px-SimonTempleman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6e/Simon